# Tests

How to write them: @.claude/skills/writing-tests/SKILL.md (parametrized tables over loops,
`*.concurrent` where isolated, which modules to mock).

- Run with `pnpm test:run`, never bare `vitest`.
- Zero network or external calls — mock `fetch`, `chrome.*`, IndexedDB, currency, analytics at
  their owning module.
- Tests that import `SupplierBase` import `ProductBuilder` first (module-init cycle).
- Test files may use `as` freely and are exempt from the TSDoc-on-every-function rule.
- Never run, so a green suite says nothing about them: `src/helpers/__tests__/productBuilder.test.ts`,
  `src/suppliers/__tests__/supplierMacklin.test.ts`, `src/__tests__/**`.
- `pnpm test:e2e:firefox` is a load smoke test only.

## Coverage limit

`configs/vitest.config.ts` sets `coverage.thresholds`; `pnpm test:coverage` and the coverage CI
workflow fail below them.

- New or changed code needs tests that keep every metric at or above its threshold.
- Never lower a threshold to make a run pass. When coverage rises, raise the thresholds to the
  new floor.
